    -> results/e2a_fixed_resolution.csv
     A row whose units/s is far below the others never reached full
     speed: at that size the fixed cost of one backward pass -- the
     grid, the array allocations, 12 x L Python-level calls --
     outweighs the arithmetic, so its time ratio understates the
     true growth.  No fixed resolution avoids this: one that is
     compute-bound at d=2 is out of reach at d=6.

